.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-GET-APPLICATION 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-get-application \- show one application's definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eap get-application
.BR \-\-application\-id | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows one application's full definition - runtime, bucket and artifact
key, command and arguments, environment, the identity it runs as,
autoscaler bounds and readiness timeout - together with how many
instances of it are running.
.PP
The environment shown is what the definition carries. It is not the whole
environment a process gets: the manager adds the \fIEUCLID_*\fR variables
described in
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
including the application's credentials, which are never printed here.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-application\-id " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the application. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The definition is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, or no application of that name exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap get-application --application-id inbox
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-list-applications (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-update-application (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
